# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit the filled version.

# ─── LiveKit transport ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Free self-hosted path: run `livekit-server --dev` (open source, Apache 2.0) and
# use its built-in dev credentials. Localhost only — never expose devkey/secret.
LIVEKIT_URL=ws://localhost:7880
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=devkey
LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=secret
# Paid path: a LiveKit Cloud project (wss://your-project.livekit.cloud) + its keys.

# ─── The tutor brain ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# openai → GPT-6 Luna for live turns and GPT-5.6 Terra for careful background work.
#   Needs one ordinary OPENAI_API_KEY. Override either model below if needed.
# groq  → an OpenAI-compatible model on Groq's free tier (console.groq.com). $0.
# anthropic → Claude, the production brain. Needs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
# claude-cli → Claude through the `claude` command, on your own subscription, so
#   the coaching can be judged before buying a key. It splits: memory, curation
#   and drill authoring go to Claude, and realtime turns stay on Groq, because a
#   command-line call costs about eight seconds and a learner would spend every
#   one of them in silence. Needs GROQ_API_KEY and `claude` on PATH; no
#   Anthropic key at all. Moving to the API later is this line and nothing else.
# claude-cli-all → subscription for the conversation brain, the learner's turn
#   included. Development only: every turn takes eight to twelve seconds, and in
#   voice mode that silence is real. It exists because a free-tier fallback
#   rate-limits a real conversation. Needs `claude` on PATH; scripted lessons
#   still require GROQ_API_KEY.
TUTOR_LLM=openai
GROQ_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_LIVE_MODEL=gpt-6-luna
# Priority processing roughly halves the wait before the tutor speaks on gpt-6-luna.
# Billed at OpenAI's higher priority rate; unset means the standard tier.
# OPENAI_LIVE_SERVICE_TIER=priority
# Written checks (the own-words judge) only. Curation has its own knob below (VOICE-012, 2026-10-24).
# OPENAI_TURN_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna
# Memory extraction only. Drills have their own knob below (VOICE-008, 2026-10-23).
# OPENAI_ANALYST_MODEL=gpt-5.6-terra
# OPENAI_DRILLS_MODEL=gpt-6-luna
# Practice curation (the five phrases kept); default gpt-6-luna.
# OPENAI_CURATION_MODEL=gpt-6-luna
# TypeSafe Jev. Optional, and the same key the token server takes. The agent
# builds its brain the same way, so it runs Jev-first too. Today only the
# own-words check makes a call Jev can settle, and that runs on the token
# server, so live sessions behave exactly as they do without it.
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
# Optional can-do quote selector: keep 0. A reviewed real-French calibration
# artifact is also required; key presence or setting 1 alone cannot enable it.
LUVANI_CAN_DO_EVIDENCE=0
# Which model on Groq. Leave unset for the current default. Groq retires models
# without warning and answers a request for a retired one with a bare 404, which
# reaches a learner as a tutor that joins and never speaks — so if the tutor goes
# silent, check this first against https://console.groq.com/docs/models.
# GROQ_MODEL=

# ─── Speech to text ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The hardest part of this pipeline. Learner French is mangled French, and a
# transcriber that silently "corrects" it destroys the pronunciation signal.
# Measure word error rate on real beginner audio before trusting this.
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=

# ─── Which voice vendor ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave this line commented out unless you mean it. Unset, blank, or any value
# the worker does not recognise all mean ElevenLabs, which is the default and
# the vendor every warmed WAV on disk is keyed to. Switching vendors re-keys the
# whole cache, so the first session on a new vendor pays for every line again.
#
# fish → fish.audio. It exists here for one reason: a native French voice its
#   free tier will actually synthesize. ElevenLabs' French voices are all
#   library or cloned voices and a free account cannot use either over the API,
#   which is why the tutor — a man from Lyon — has been speaking in an American
#   woman's voice. Needs FISH_API_KEY and FISH_VOICE_ID below.
#
# Deliberately commented rather than shipped blank: `TUTOR_LLM=` taught us that
# an empty line reads as "unset" to a human and as "set" to `??`, and that cost
# a debugging session.
# LUVANI_TTS_VENDOR=fish

# ─── French voice: ElevenLabs (the default) ───────────────────────────────────
# The dominant audio cost line (currently about $0.05/1k characters, roughly
# $0.05/minute of generated speech). If margins bite, the first move is premium
# voice for conversation and a cheaper voice for repeated drills.
ELEVEN_API_KEY=
#
# THERE IS NO VOICE VARIABLE HERE ANY MORE, and that is the point of this block.
# The learner chooses their tutor's voice in Profile, from eight voices listed
# in packages/core/src/protocol/voices.ts. The catalogue keys are ours
# (luc, alexandre, enrick, mathieu, guillaume, benoit, celine, emilie) and the
# vendor ids they map to live in ELEVEN_VOICES in src/voice.ts, which is the
# only file that holds them, because this is the only process that holds the key
# above. Luc is who a learner gets before they have chosen.
#
# ELEVEN_VOICE_ID is RETIRED. If it is still in your .env, delete the line:
# nothing reads it, and preflight will say so on every boot. Leaving it there is
# worse than an empty variable, because a real vendor id under a dead name reads
# to the next person as "this is the voice the tutor uses".
#
# Every one of the eight must be a voice the vendor lists as VERIFIED FOR FRENCH
# AND FOR ENGLISH on the model pinned in src/voice.ts, which is
# eleven_multilingual_v2. Check that pairing against /v2/voices
# verified_languages before adding a ninth: a voice verified for French on turbo
# and not on multilingual reproduces, mirrored, the bug that had the tutor
# speaking months of out-of-distribution French. English matters as much as
# French — the same voice speaks the opener, the narration and every coaching
# line, and a French accent on those is correct and wanted, because it is one
# person and not two.
#
# REQUIRES A PAID ELEVENLABS PLAN. Every native French voice is a library or
# cloned voice, and the free tier refuses both over the API ("Free users cannot
# use library voices via the API"). The free tier's own premade voices are all
# English. So a native French tutor is a paid line item, not a config choice.
# Preflight proves on every boot that this account still lists all eight, and
# names the key to fix when one has gone.

# ─── French voice: fish.audio (only read when LUVANI_TTS_VENDOR=fish) ──────────
# FISH_API_KEY is the name the plugin reads, and it is the only one it reads.
# FISH_AUDIO_API_KEY is the near-miss preflight will warn you about, because it
# is the name this key was first pasted under and a value under a name nothing
# reads is worse than an empty one.
# FISH_API_KEY=
#
# SET THIS, or the tutor speaks in fish's own default voice — "Sarah", a young
# American woman, which is the exact voice this vendor was added to escape.
# Preflight warns when it is unset, and the warning is not decoration.
# FISH_VOICE_ID=
#
# Which model. This is a BILL, not a preference. fish sends the model as an HTTP
# header, and an omitted or unrecognised one falls back to the paid s2.1-pro at
# roughly $15 per million UTF-8 bytes — verified: omitting it returns 402 on a
# zero-credit account. Unset here means s2.1-pro-free, the only model the free
# tier serves, whose free window was published to end 2026-08-31. When it closes
# this starts answering 402 on every boot and preflight will say so; s2-pro is
# the paid escape.
# FISH_MODEL=s2.1-pro-free

# ─── Pronunciation scoring ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. With nothing here the session still runs, and the end card says
# plainly that nothing was scored rather than inventing a focus.
#
# The live-session switch. Set to 1 to score each captured learner utterance in
# a scripted lesson. Scoring runs beside the reply, never in front of it (F623,
# VOICE-004): the tutor answers at once and the score joins the end card when it
# lands. Only a learner who said the lesson's reference line is scored. In
# production the vendor must be Speechace (preflight), reached through the paid
# gate with audio converted in process, so the lesson binding in
# LUVANI_PAID_QUOTE_BINDINGS must declare kinds including scoring (F863;
# deployment/PAID_ADMISSION.md). Off by default until a real-learner run
# has been reviewed. Drills and sound checks are scored by the token server,
# which does not read it.
# LUVANI_AUDIO_SCORING=1

# Conversation-only ASR review candidate; keep OFF until real beginner and room QA.
# Uses Flux Multilingual with French/English hints; synthetic evidence is insufficient
# to replace the normal Nova-3 scene recognizer. Does not affect lessons or typing.
LUVANI_CONVO_ASR_EXPERIMENT=0
#
# The scorer. TonePerfect is the default whenever its key is set, and
# services/shared/pronunciation.ts is where the choice is made. This worker
# reads it only while LUVANI_AUDIO_SCORING=1. Server-side only.
# TONEPERFECT_API_KEY=
#
# Which vendor scores: toneperfect or speechace. Unset means TonePerfect when its
# key is set, else Speechace when its key is. A vendor named here without its
# key scores nothing: the learner's audio is never sent to the other one.
# Commented rather than shipped blank, for the same reason as LUVANI_TTS_VENDOR.
# LUVANI_SCORING_VENDOR=speechace
#
# The alternative scorer, used when it is named above or is the only key set.
# SPEECHACE_API_KEY=

# ─── Talking to the token server ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Must match LUVANI_AGENT_SECRET in services/token-server/.env. Without it the
# debit endpoint is open to anyone who can reach it.
# LUVANI_AGENT_SECRET=

# ─── Latency knobs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All three exist, all three default to off, and none of them was documented
# here until the tutor was measured.
#
# How a TTS cache miss reaches the vendor. `ws` uses the vendor's persistent
# pooled websocket, sparing every sentence a fresh TLS handshake before its
# first audio byte. In free conversation nearly every sentence is a miss, so
# this is the biggest per-sentence win on offer. The default stays `http`
# because the standalone warm-cache script must be free to exit the moment the
# last line lands rather than dangle on an idle vendor socket.
# LUVANI_TTS_MISS_TRANSPORT=ws
#
# Free-conversation voice model. Off when unset. eleven_flash_v2_5 is the only
# accepted value, and anything else stops the worker at startup. When on, only
# free-conversation lines go to Flash (about half the price per character);
# every scripted line and the warm cache stay on eleven_multilingual_v2. Same
# voice, settings and format. ElevenLabs only: ignored under fish. In
# production the TTS quote must price an eleven_flash_v2_5 component first
# (deployment/PAID_ADMISSION.md), or conversation lines are refused.
# LUVANI_CONVERSATION_TTS_MODEL=eleven_flash_v2_5
# The default cache lives inside this checkout. Point this at one persistent
# absolute directory when testing from disposable Git worktrees, otherwise each
# worktree starts cold even when another checkout has already warmed the voice.
# TTS_CACHE_DIR=/absolute/path/to/luvani-tts-cache
#
# Turn taking. No turn-detector plugin is installed, so the framework already
# uses plain silence-based VAD and this selects what is happening anyway. It is
# here as the seam for latency A/B work, and for the day the plugin is added.
# LUVANI_TURN_DETECTION=vad
#
# Kill switches, both on by default. LUVANI_SESSION_HEADS_UP=0 drops the
# spoken heads-up a minute before the cap and the warm close (sessionEnd.ts),
# leaving only the hard stop. LUVANI_TAP_TO_SEND=0 makes the worker ignore the
# app's tap-to-send switch and Send, so turns stay automatic (tapToSend.ts).
# LUVANI_SESSION_HEADS_UP=0
# LUVANI_TAP_TO_SEND=0
#
# How hard every brain activity thinks. Moves all five together (turn, frame,
# extract, drills, curate); see packages/brain/src/llm/routing.ts for the table
# it overrides. Lowering it trades coaching quality for turn latency.
# BRAIN_EFFORT=low

# Explicit typing-only recovery: set to 1 in BOTH agent and token-server envs.
# Spoken session starts are refused; brain and LiveKit credentials remain required.
LUVANI_TYPED_ONLY=0

# Optional authored Why? link: requires a reviewed real-French calibration
# artifact with its own probability threshold. No approved artifact exists.
LUVANI_CORRECTION_REASONS=0

# Experimental exact worker TTS-frame timing. No phone-audible measurement.
# Keep off until queued SDK correlation and bounded voice proof are reviewed.
LUVANI_REPLY_FIRST_FRAME_TIMING=0

# Stream live conversation turns so the reply is spoken as soon as its fields
# are in (VOICE-003, OpenAI brain only). Set to 0 to revert to one JSON body
# per turn without a deploy of new code.
LUVANI_STREAM_TURN=1

# Speech dataset seam: off, and inert until legal review (docs/changes/speech-dataset.md).
# Also needs LUVANI_AUDIO_SCORING=1 and the learner's consent, which nothing sets today.
# LUVANI_SPEECH_DATASET=1
